[?2004l not [?2004h>             "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004lion du[?2004h>             "answer": "The safety risks listed for Paxlovid include drug-drug interactions (which can lead to serious, life-threatening, or fatal events), hypersensitivity reactions (including anaphylaxis, toxic epidermal necrolysis, and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), hepatotoxicity (hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice), and risk of HIV-1 resistance development. In clinical trials, the most common adverse reactions (>=1% incidence and more frequent than placebo) were dysgeusia and diarrhea. Other post-authorization adverse reactions include headache, hypertension, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and malaise.",
[?2004l[?2004h>             "citations": [
