[?2004l[?2004h>         {
[?2004l[?2004h>             "qid": "cf74a5a8ac9b19de",
[?2004l[?2004h>             "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>             "answer": "Paxlovid is contraindicated in: 1) Patients with a history of clinically significant hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., toxic epidermal necrolysis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome) to its active ingredients (nirmatrelvir or ritonavir) or other components; 2) Concomitant use with drugs primarily metabolized by CYP3A for which elevated concentrations are associated with serious and/or life-threatening reactions (e.g., alfuzosin, ranolazine, amiodarone, dronedarone, flecainide, propafenone, quinidine, colchicine in renal/hepatic impairment, lurasidone, pimozide, silodosin, eplerenone, ivabradine, dihydroergotamine, ergotamine, methylergonovine, lovastatin, simvastatin, voclosporin, lomitapide, eletriptan, ubrogepant, finerenone, naloxegol, sildenafil for PAH, triazolam, oral midazolam, flibanserin, and tolvaptan); and 3) Concomitant use with strong CYP3A inducers where significantly reduced plasma concentrations of Paxlovid may cause loss of virologic response and possible resistance (e.g., apalutamide, enzalutamide, carbamazepine, phenobarbital, primidone, phenytoin, rifampin, rifapentine, lumacaftor/ivacaftor, and St. John's Wort).",
[?2004l[?2004h>             "citations": [
