[?2004l[?2004h>             "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>             "answer": "Paxlovid should not be taken by: 1) Patients with a history of clinically significant hypersensitivity reactions (such as toxic epidermal necrolysis or Stevens-Johnson syndrome) to nirmatrelvir, ritonavir, or any other component of the product; 2) Patients taking any of the contraindicated medications that are highly dependent on CYP3A for clearance or are strong CYP3A inducers; and 3) Patients with severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh Class C), as Paxlovid is not recommended for this population due to a lack of pharmacokinetic or safety data.",
